hese moves expand to the right. (F, 7) is reasonable but places a piece adjacent to the dangerous corner zones on the right side.\n- **(B, 4)**: This is an internal move that flips three of the opponent\'s central pieces (C4, D4, E4). It does not touch the edges or corners, keeping the game tight and preserving good structural shape.\n\nReason: I choose (B, 4) because it is a safe, central move that improves my position by flipping internal opponent pieces ("evaporation" strategy) without exposing any corners or weak edges. It minimizes the risk of the opponent gaining a positional advantage in the next turn compared to the high-variance edge move at A5 or the corner-adjacent moves on the right.\n\nAnswer: (B, 4)'}
