ly respond with (E, 7), which would flip D7 back to their color.\n- Move (E, 7): This move is disadvantageous because it places a piece adjacent to the empty E8 square, allowing the opponent to play (E, 8) and capture the entire E row (E3-E7).\n\nReason: Playing (A, 7) initiates the optimal sequence (Me A7 -> Opponent E7 -> Me E8). This order allows me to secure the top edge immediately and the right edge on my final turn. Crucially, by playing (E, 8) last, I capture the internal piece D7 and keep it, whereas playing (E, 8) first would result in D7 being flipped back by the opponent's subsequent move. This sequence maximizes the final piece count.\n\nAnswer: (A, 7)"}
